'\" t
.TH IMUD\-MON 1 "2026-07-20" "imud 1.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imud\-mon \- live monitor for imud output streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud-mon
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fBnmea\fR]
[\fBbinary\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud-mon
listens on the UDP ports configured for
.BR imud (8)
and prints a live, updating display of the received data.
The display refreshes once per second.
.PP
By default both streams are monitored simultaneously.
Pass one or more stream names as arguments to restrict to those streams.
.PP
Each stream section shows:
.PP
.RS 4
.TP
.B NMEA
Heading, pitch, and roll parsed from
.BR $PASHR ,
rate of turn from
.BR $TIROT ,
true heading from
.B $HCHDT
(when available), and the last received sentence.
.TP
.B Binary
All fields from the high-rate binary packet: heading, pitch, roll,
rate of turn, quaternion, calibrated and raw gyro/accel/mag vectors,
covariance, declination, and status flags.
.RE
.PP
Status flags are shown as a compact string.
Each character represents a flag:
.TS
l l.
C	Fusion filter converged
V	Magnetometer reading valid (not rejected)
A	Accelerometer calibration loaded
G	Gyroscope calibration loaded
M	Magnetometer calibration loaded
D	Declination valid; true heading available
S	Startup / settling period active
!	IMU FIFO overflow since the last packet
.TE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ PATH
Config file used to determine UDP ports and addresses to listen on.
Defaults to
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
(then
.IR ~/.config/imud/imud.conf ).
.TP
.B nmea
Monitor only the NMEA stream.
.TP
.B binary
Monitor only the high-rate binary stream.
.SH EXAMPLES
Monitor both streams:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-mon
.EE
.RE
.PP
Monitor NMEA only:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-mon nmea
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use a non-default config (e.g.\& sim mode):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-mon --config config/sim.conf
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud-status (1),
.BR imud.conf (5)
.SH AUTHORS
Richard Simpson
